# .bivignore — bivpak (product code repo)
#
# WHY .git IS EXCLUDED — read before removing this rule.
# `biv pack` REFUSES outright on any directory containing a `.git` entry
# (typed RepoDiscoveredUnsupported, src/core/scan/scan.cpp) because the git
# engine is ROADMAP Step 4 and is not implemented. The ignore matcher runs
# BEFORE that refusal, so pruning `.git` is what makes this repo packable at
# all. Without this rule, `biv pack .` fails immediately.
#
# Unlike pdc, this repo HAS a remote (github.com/iwnlcern/bivpak), so history
# is recoverable by clone on the far side — push any live branch first.
.git/

# Build output — 645 MB of the repo's 695 MB. Excluding this is the difference
# between a portable image and an unusable one. Binaries are rebuilt from
# source on the target host; they are not portable across OS/arch anyway.
build/

# Python virtualenv — 32 MB, machine- AND interpreter-specific (absolute paths
# baked into bin/ shims). Rebuild on the target with:
#   python3 -m venv .venv-harness && .venv-harness/bin/pip install -r harness/requirements.lock
.venv-harness/

# Transient / machine-local
.DS_Store
*.swp
compile_commands.json
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
